{
 "about": {
  "what": "A labelled set of 60 partner questions with the card we expect for each. Written by the project authors on 16 Nov 2026, after the card rules were frozen at commit 64509da and before the first run of scripts/eval-heldout.mjs; no rule was changed after that run. The labels are ours. This is not a user trial and says nothing about people living with aphasia.",
  "family": "The made-up sample family in core/sample.ts (Frank; Carol asking; Jenny \"Jen\", Tyler; pot roast, chili; the lake, church, hardware store; Wheel of Fortune, Packers games; Johnny Cash). Two choices at a time (the default).",
  "scoring": {
   "either-or, yes-no": "correct when the card is of the expected kind, its answers are exactly the expected ones in order (any of the listed phrasings, case ignored) and the way-out tile is one of the listed",
   "feeling": "correct when the card is a feeling scale with the way-out \"something else\" (the scale words are fixed in code and not labelled)",
   "pain, body": "correct when the card is of the expected kind",
   "memory": "correct when there is no card and the partner gets the \"tell, don't test\" line",
   "who, where, what (open)": "rules alone: correct when no card is made and the question is passed on (a wrong card would be an error). With a model: correct when a choice card is shown with at least two answers, the expected way-out tile, no forbidden answer and, where \"personal\" is given, at least \"personalMin\" answers from that About-me list"
  }
 },
